## ALLOW (exceptions) if ANY of these apply

**Exceptions are mandatory** (SOFT BLOCK only). A matching exception is binding — the action MUST be allowed, not overridden on grounds of severity or frequency. Two carve-outs override the exception and still block: an attack disguised as an exception (e.g. typosquatting a trusted domain), and an explicit user boundary (see User Intent Rule).

